! The porch ~ the sweeper's kit

The operator ruled on 2026-10-26 to close open work before the founding bake. This lane sweeps the road's hygiene pile (burned-name guards, evergreen remainders, tests-only debts, re-measures and canon sweeps) beside the slotted lanes, in small trains: each bundle lands off the span head, and the controller writes the road at each land. The crew stands as <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes">>: one walled Sol builder, one walled Luna reader and sweeper, the lead running every suite.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-one>>

!! Bundle one ~ three tooling items and the burned-name guards

!!! The Playwright engine cache
* ''A CDN stall once held a runner for 20 minutes and for 48.'' Every job in `.github/workflows` that installs engines (`ci.yml`'s browser-vessel suite, floor crossing and standalone single-file suite; `held-out.yml`'s browser-weld cell) now restores `~/.cache/ms-playwright` keyed on the runner OS, the Playwright version `pnpm exec playwright --version` names, and the engine set. The install step still runs for the system libraries and downloads only on a miss. A version bump re-downloads once.
* ''Stays.'' The TiddlyWiki5 submodule's own `bin/ci-test.sh` installs engines for upstream's CI, outside this repository's workflows.

!!! The household witness image
* ''`household-https-witness` builds `lares-surface:local` from this tree on every run'' when `HOUSEHOLD_IMAGE` stands unset, so a stale local tag never meets newer code (the layer cache keeps an unchanged tree cheap). A set `HOUSEHOLD_IMAGE` reads as given and builds only when the tag stands absent.
* ''Stays.'' `tools/harbor-walk-witness.sh` keeps the same absent-only build (`HARBOR_IMAGE`); it wants the same line when its next owner touches it.

!!! The `custody-frames` U1 leak
* ''The cause.'' U1's control read `loadActivePersonaIndex().catch(() => undefined)`. That reader infers the one face standing open, and it opens the seated custody, which refuses outside a scratch root. Under a real `HOME` the refusal fell into the `catch` and the assertion read green by accident; under a scratch `HOME` or `LAR_ROOT` the custody opened, an earlier vector's face stood open, and the reader answered `0`.
* ''The cure.'' The control reads the composition's own choice (`mountedFaceOrdinal()`), the thing the unlock frame sets, and the file reads green under a real `HOME` and under a scratch `HOME` with a scratch `LAR_ROOT`. The test title no longer claims a case it never asserted: an unlock naming no face mounts the vessel's one face by the door's own rule.

!!! Burned-name guards burned
* `lar-wire.test.ts`: the control that `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` pass no door (road `F8`).
* `browser-walk.test.ts`: the control that the `boot-invite-burned`, `hosting-walk` and `nexus-keys` stores stand absent (road `W20`).
* `vessel-wipe-surfaces.test.ts`, now `vessel-surfaces.test.ts`: the `vessel clear`, `rite rebirth` and `--clear` refusals and the negative help checks; the live `read`, refresh and surface-table assertions stay.
* `nexus-verb-reach.test.ts`: `nexus refresh` reads as an unknown verb.
* `vault-door.test.ts`: the former vault verbs (`seal`, `rotate`, `repair`, `passphrase`, `export`), `--yes`, `--check` and the passphrase environment route; the exact seven-verb help assertion and a nonsense-verb refusal stay.
* `cabal-realm-ceremony.test.ts`: the absent-export list for the former eviction and closing API; the exact live export assertion stays.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-two>>

!! Bundle two ~ the stream manifest, the witness image, the leak and the readings

!!! Closed
* ''`G38` The stream manifest stands as one shape in both languages.'' The Python writer (`sensorium.py`) declares `lifecycle` in every stream manifest: it mirrors `deriveLifecycle` at mint, `set_stream_ephemeral` recomputes it when `ephemeral` flips, and a declared `tombstone` stays. The reader (`sensorium.ts`) requires a declared state and refuses an absent one by name; the derivation fallback burned. The builder keeps its mint-time default, which writes the field. Python tests pin the writer and the setter; the node tests pin the refusal beside its control.
* ''`tools/harbor-walk-witness.sh` builds from the tree'' with `HARBOR_IMAGE` unset, as the household witness does.
* ''The `held-out-steps` test names its actor.'' The plan test read `git config user.name`, which a scratch `HOME` lacks; it now names `GITHUB_ACTOR` as the runner does, and the file reads green under a scratch `HOME`.

!!! Readings, no change owed
* ''`H7`.'' No line in `membership-doctrine` calls an introduction's lifetime unruled any longer. `#/the-invite` states that the answer consumes the introduction, that the three dials count and read no clock, and that a posture names a setting and never a date. The strike belongs to the road.
* ''`G19` carriers read true against the code at this head.'' The five sweeps met no disagreeing line:
** `docker-compose.mesh.yml` and `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml` both state that the localhost exemption is not TLS and cite each other;
** `secure-context#/behind-the-terminator` and `harbor#/household-https` agree on `LAR_PUBLIC_URL`, loopback publication and the scheme;
** the test door's marker (`.lar-test-scratch`) and the suites' temp-dir check (`scratch-custody-setup.ts`) stand as two named things, and no carrier merges them.
* ''`kahu.mem` and `lamplighters.mem` on what the code holds'' needs a reader who holds the operator's intent for the cadence share. It stays on `G19` for the controller.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-three>>

!! Bundle three ~ the harness image, the marker test, the flush reading and the carried items

!!! Closed
* ''`A9` The browser harness stands as an image.'' `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml`'s `qa` runner builds the `browser-harness` Dockerfile target: the pinned Playwright client, the two browser walks (`browser-ci-smoke.mjs`, `live-wiki.mjs`), their join helper and the built custody probe, and no repository bind (the `/exchange` bind and the tmpfs stay). `tools/browser-ci.sh` builds the image when absent. `harness-image-law` scans the `qa` service and the target, with the old bind planted as its red control; the mesh's `browser-a` and `browser-b` stay its two named exceptions. The target built and ran on this host: Playwright imports in the image, and the walks and probe sit where the walks look for them.
* ''`G17` The node daemon's scratch marker admits nothing.'' Canon rules it (`harbor` (the container boundary and the test custody door)): every boot rests at the floor holding no vessel key, and a harness opens a staged vessel through the test custody door alone. `test-scratch-marker-admission.test.ts` pins that a marked root yields the TEST SCRATCH notice, an unmarked root yields none, and after the notice the seated holder stays locked and a sealed row refuses at the floor. `main.ts` calls the extracted `testScratchNotice`.
* ''`G8` The per-verb flush stands measured, and its instrument is `tools/flush-bench.mjs`.'' A verb ends at its awaited `flush([document])`; the bench times that call as a microbenchmark, a one-field change to a synthetic document in a `Repo` over the product's store adapter (`DurableNodeFSStorageAdapter`), and dispatches no product verb. One reading, 2026-10-27, Node 24, the 443 carriers under `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba` resident as 443 documents: per-verb flush p50 5.7 ms, p95 8.2 ms, p99 11.7 ms, max 13.5 ms (n = 443); the one-document control reads p50 4.5 ms, p95 6.3 ms (n = 100). The whole-repo `flush()` that names no document reads p50 15.6 ms, p95 24.5 ms (n = 20). So a verb that names its document pays about a millisecond over the control at full corpus, and a flush that names none pays about three times that. The first flush of the loaded corpus took 0.9 s. A planted-set test (`flush-bench.test.mjs`) reads the arithmetic before any reading trusts it, and the bench refuses a corpus under 400 carriers.
* ''`G20` the sensorium `requirements.txt` tree-sitter pins.'' The binding pin (`tree-sitter==0.26.0`) is the newest the index holds; the carrier grammar generates ABI 15, inside the binding's 13 to 15 window. `test_tree_sitter_pins.py` holds that pair to the tree, with a planted out-of-window control, and the pin equals the installed binding.
* ''`G20` the Elyncia carrier that failed the corpus round-trip.'' At this head the round-trip law holds for every carrier under `bags/`. `meme-corpus-roundtrip.test.ts` now sweeps all of `bags/` (the six bags, 778 carriers) in place of the lares bag alone, and a second test fails by name on any carrier the law skips by shape. The carrier is no longer unowned: the standing law owns it.
* The sensorium conftest exempts `ANONYMIZED_TELEMETRY` as the third-party one-shot the mempalace package stamps on first import. Whichever test imported it first used to carry the blame.

!!! Stays, with its reason
* ''`G20` the cold-boot `unavailable` reading.'' The per-source map reads as follows. `findWithProgress` (automerge-repo 2.6.0-alpha.5, `DocumentQuery`) answers `unavailable` once no source is pending and the handle holds no data, and the state carries a `sources` map (`storage`, `automerge-sync`). A hearth-private doc has no peer to wait on, so `unavailable` reads terminal; the one case it misreads is a write this vessel has issued and not yet rested. `boot-resolver.ts` covers that case with a two-second grace on a monotonic clock. A clock decides there, which the house law forbids, and the cure is the writer's own event: the caller names the flush it owes (`repo.flush([id])`) and the resolver asks again after it settles. The production caller that needs it is `open-node-vessel.ts` (`readDaemonDoc`), K15's file, and `K15`'s bonds (PR #106) built that cure: `resolveBootDoc` takes an optional `settled`, `readDaemonDoc` passes the Repo's flush, and `UNAVAILABLE_GRACE_MS` retired.
* ''`G8` pack-PIN recursion and the `assertBodyIndexTier` caller.'' Pack-PIN recursion stays unbuilt (`blob-carriage#/proposed-law`); the tier caller arrives with the cad body-index writer, since `bodyIndexBagUri` has no producer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/rulings-owed>>

!! Rulings owed, each with options and one lean

* ''`G20` road (iv) with surface-for-review.'' Road (iv) is a quorum-membership change, where the board records derive which admits and offices leaned on a departed signer and the new quorum reviews them (`lamplighters.mem` near line 205, `kahu.mem` lines 431 to 437). No code builds it, and the canon rule says a seat change re-seats nothing. Options: (a) surface the derived set as information and let the quorum revoke by name on the deny board; (b) keep the set as a tracked review queue with explicit closure; (c) automate revocation, which breaks the non-cascade rule. Lean: (a).
* ''`G20` loans keyed by CID.'' A loan is a time-bounded ADD that reverts, and `effect-record.ts` lists it TTL-pending. Residency keys by title and bag; blob bytes key by CID. Options: (a) loan by title and bag, which repeats a grant for each reference; (b) loan by CID with the holder and tier kept, so the grant follows the bytes and keeps its scope; (c) loan by CID alone, which grants across unrelated holders. The TTL itself needs a clockless form first. Lean: (b), after the loan has a causal expiry.
* ''`G20` the `/cas` timing call.'' The `/cas` read face (`bulb-read-face.ts`) authorizes each request against the public index and then reads bytes; the open question is the order in which a body and its public index land. Options: (a) land and verify the body, then the index, so no public reference dangles; (b) index first, so a reference may meet a missing body; (c) stage both and expose the index at one commit. A clock decides none of the three. Lean: (a), unless an atomic publication boundary already stands.
* ''`G20` the parallel-draft alert's persistence'' belongs to the hands room, where drafts and alerts live. The porch names that owner and builds nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-stays>>

!! What stays, and why

* ''`projection-input-leg.test.ts` (road `F8`).'' It guards `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` as unclaimed. It belongs to D2's tw5 projection test surface; it burns when D2 lands.
* ''The CLI unknown-command list and the keyhive cabal names (road `W20`).'' The unknown-command refusal is generic and tests with a nonsense control; no named cabal guard remains outside the held modules (`ceremony-core.ts`, `keyhive-provider.ts`, `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`, K15).
* ''Bundle four stands unbuilt, and the porch rests.'' Codex credits ran out and the operator called a rest on 2026-10-27, so a fresh crew takes it. Four items, each with its ruling and its first reading:
** ''`G6` outside the two vessel files.'' Stale prose, back-compat wording and tolerant readers in `nexus-seal-seed.ts`, `seed-wrap-prf.ts`, `ingest-core.ts`, `lar-uris.ts` and `mesh-palace.ts`; `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` wait for K15; `cleanup-days.ts` stays unlocated. Instrument: `node tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` and its EXCEPTIONS (each names its owner). Check each file against the live lanes before editing.
** ''Road (iv), ruled 2026-10-27.'' On a quorum-membership change, derive from the board records which admits and offices leaned on a departed signer and surface that impact set for review as information. Nothing cascades; a quorum revokes by name on the deny board. Canon: `lamplighters.mem` near line 205 and `kahu.mem` lines 431 to 437. First read: the board readers, the seat-change and roll path, where a departed signer is known, and where a reviewer reads the set (a CLI command, a verb or a field on an existing status). Size it before building; write a lane brief if it passes a bundle.
** ''Loans keyed by CID, ruled 2026-10-27.'' A loan keys by CID and keeps its holder and tier, once it carries a causal expiry counted in rolls or epochs (`blob-carriage#/proposed-law` counts a grace in realm rolls). `effect-record.ts` lists `loan` TTL-pending; `residency-model.mem` line 154 defines the loan. The expiry comes first, and a clock never decides it. Write a lane brief if the expiry design passes a bundle.
** ''`/cas` order, ruled 2026-10-27.'' The body lands and verifies before the public index names it. `bulb-read-face.ts` serves `/cas` after `publicCas.isPublic(cid)`. First read: every writer that lands a body and names it in the public index (`publicCas`, `content-handle.ts`, `bodyIndexBagUri`, which has no production producer today), then where the ordering is enforced and a red test that names a CID before its body verified.
* ''Also left.'' `G8` pack-PIN recursion and the `assertBodyIndexTier` caller (it arrives with the cad body-index writer); `F8`'s `projection-input-leg.test.ts` guard (D2 burns it); the K15-held `W20` names; the cold-boot grace (K15 bonds); the parallel-draft alert (hands room); the `kahu.mem` and `lamplighters.mem` sweep on `G19` (needs the operator's cadence-share intent); the `harness-image-law` and flush-bench instruments stay as built.

<<~/ahu>>

